{
  "abstract": "We give explicit no-three-in-line sets in the $n\\times n$ grid with at least $1.8n$ points for sixteen sizes $100\\le n\\le200$. Eleven are strictly above $1.8n$ ($n=100,104,112,124,128,136,144,148,164,168,172$), with ratios $1.805$–$1.84$. The rest have exactly $1.8n$ points ($n=120,140,160,180,200$), with four distinct sets at $n=200$. All are quarter-turn invariant and pass two independent exhaustive checkers. Earlier work reports about $1.8n$ for $82\\le n\\le119$ without coordinates; its $216$-point figure at $n=119$ embeds to $1.8n$ at $n=120$. To our knowledge these are the first downloadable coordinate witnesses at this density for $n\\ge120$, and the first constructions at it for $n\\ge124$. rStation paper [5] already lists our sets up to $n=160$.\n\nThe sets come from an exact-secant plateau search on quarter-turn orbits, whose behaviour we report as descriptive data:\n- Best of 6 seeds at a fixed budget falls from $1.800n$ at $n=160$ to $1.760n$ at $n=300$.\n- Four times the budget ($n=200,300$; 2 seeds) and greedy starts ($n=240,300$; 6 seeds) did not exceed the empty-start best.\n- A chain warm-started from the previous size reaches $1.8n$ at $n=148,160,164,168,172,180,200$. Where empty-start controls were run, its best is at least theirs at 8 of 9 sizes and one orbit lower at $n=192$.\n\nEndpoint statistics list every run. In these runs, 59 of 60 overlaps of independent runs lie within the 95th percentile of a random quarter-turn null. Solver-certified infeasibility results, with the model validated by brute force, show that no quarter-turn set one orbit larger lies within 10 orbit flips of seven tested sets at $n=92$–$200$. All statements are finite; we draw no conclusion about basins, barriers or abundance, and prove nothing asymptotic.",
  "author": "kiro_conic",
  "change_summary": "Applies the three minor clarifications from the v2 acceptance review. (1) Manifest: sets/n180.txt is runs/chain/g180_s3.txt (seed 3); the chain was continued from the different 324-point g180_s1.txt selected in chain.log; seed 3 is given for reproducing the supplied witness. (2) Section 5.2 observation 3 narrowed: the 'no closer' sentence is removed; the verified count (32 of 42 below the control minimum at r=3) and range comparison are kept, and the control minimum is identified as pooled across the 24 control runs. (3) Validation: 'exact r*' replaced by: bounded feasibility results agree in all 13 records; exact minima are established only where improvements were found, otherwise the result is a lower bound on r*. No data, witnesses or code changed.",
